---
/**
 * An author’s note, inverted onto midnight so it stands apart from the paper
 * sections around it. Credentials stated flatly for the skeptic, warmth
 * second. The portrait and the book cover sit as captioned plates hanging
 * toward the right margin.
 */
---

<section
	class="teacher-section grain grain--overlay"
	id="teacher"
	aria-labelledby="teacher-heading"
>
	<div class="sheet">
		<span class="label-caps sheet-margin">The teacher</span>

		<div class="teacher-layout sheet-wide">
			<h2 id="teacher-heading" class="teacher-heading">Led by Charlie Awbery</h2>

			<div class="teacher-copy">
				<p>
					Charlie spent twenty-five years studying, practicing, and teaching Vajrayana, a
					life-affirming Buddhist path. They cofounded
					<a href="https://www.evolvingground.org/" target="_blank">Evolving Ground</a>, a community
					of contemporary practice, and wrote
					<a href="https://www.evolvingground.org/opening-awareness" target="_blank"
						><cite>Opening Awareness</cite></a
					>
					(2023), about the meditation this course teaches. These days they also teach this meditation
					to tech founders and AI researchers operating at the frontier of artificial intelligence.
				</p>
				<p>
					In the course, Charlie guides with a steady, companionable presence. Sometimes you’ll get
					clear instruction, or perhaps experiments to try or new things to notice. You get both
					clear, rooted instruction, and broad context into how this method works. They stay close
					and responsive, offering simple pointers that help you notice what’s already present.
				</p>
				<p class="teacher-provenance">
					The method is a contemporary adaptation of a practice with centuries of history in Tibetan
					traditions. The course is in plain, practical English throughout.
				</p>
			</div>

			<div class="teacher-media">
				<figure class="teacher-figure">
					<div class="teacher-portrait plate">
						<img
							src="/images/charlie-320.webp"
							srcset="/images/charlie-320.webp 320w, /images/charlie-416.webp 416w, /images/charlie-512.webp 512w"
							sizes="(max-width: 52rem) 11rem, 13rem"
							alt="Portrait of Charlie Awbery"
							loading="lazy"
							fetchpriority="low"
							decoding="async"
							width="320"
							height="320"
						/>
					</div>
					<figcaption class="caption">Charlie Awbery</figcaption>
				</figure>

				<figure class="teacher-figure teacher-figure--book">
					<a
						class="book-plate plate"
						href="https://www.evolvingground.org/opening-awareness"
						target="_blank"
						aria-label="Opening Awareness, the book, at Evolving Ground"
					>
						<img
							src="/images/opening-awareness-cover.jpg"
							alt="Cover of Opening Awareness by Charlie Awbery"
							loading="lazy"
							fetchpriority="low"
							decoding="async"
							width="348"
							height="522"
						/>
					</a>
					<figcaption class="caption"><cite>Opening Awareness</cite> (2023)</figcaption>
				</figure>
			</div>
		</div>

		<figure class="book-quote">
			<blockquote>
				This is a path of celebration, of down-to-earth realism, of uplifting courage, of gentle
				precision, and of open hearts.
			</blockquote>
			<figcaption>— <cite>Opening Awareness</cite> (2023)</figcaption>
		</figure>
	</div>
</section>

<style>
	.teacher-section {
		background: var(--surface-dark);
		color: var(--ink-on-dark);
		padding: clamp(3.5rem, 5vw + 1rem, 6.5rem) 0;
	}

	.teacher-section .label-caps {
		color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--ink-on-dark) 76%, transparent);
	}

	.teacher-layout {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: minmax(0, var(--measure)) minmax(10rem, 13rem);
		/* Row gap stays 0 so the heading's own margin sets the space below it. */
		gap: 0 clamp(2rem, 4vw, 4rem);
		align-items: start;
		padding-right: clamp(1.5rem, 3vw, 3rem);
	}

	/* The heading rides its own full-width row, so the media column starts
	   level with the first paragraph. */
	.teacher-heading {
		grid-column: 1 / -1;
		font-size: var(--fs-h2);
		font-weight: 390;
		letter-spacing: -0.018em;
		line-height: 1.1;
		text-wrap: balance;
		color: var(--ink-on-dark);
		margin: 0 0 clamp(1.25rem, 2vw, 2rem);
	}

	.teacher-copy p {
		font-size: var(--fs-body);
		line-height: var(--leading-prose);
		text-wrap: pretty;
		color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--ink-on-dark) 88%, transparent);
		margin: 0 0 var(--space-sm);
	}

	.teacher-copy p:first-of-type {
		color: var(--ink-on-dark);
	}

	.teacher-copy a {
		text-decoration: underline;
		text-decoration-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 65%, transparent);
		text-decoration-thickness: from-font;
		text-decoration-skip-ink: auto;
		text-underline-offset: 0.16em;
		transition: text-decoration-color var(--dur-hover) var(--ease-standard);
	}

	@media (hover: hover) and (pointer: fine) {
		.teacher-copy a:hover {
			text-decoration-color: var(--accent);
		}
	}

	.teacher-provenance {
		font-style: italic;
	}

	.teacher-media {
		display: grid;
		gap: 1.5rem;
	}

	/* On midnight the plates border and caption with light ink, not paper ink. */
	.teacher-media .plate {
		border-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--ink-on-dark) 32%, transparent);
	}

	.teacher-media .caption {
		color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--ink-on-dark) 76%, transparent);
		border-top: 0;
		padding-top: 0;
		text-align: center;
	}

	/* Shrink the book figure to its plate so the caption centers under it. */
	.teacher-figure--book {
		max-width: 11rem;
	}

	/* Cited title, so serif italic — the sans has no italic face and
	   font-synthesis is off. */
	.teacher-figure--book .caption {
		font-family: var(--font-serif);
		font-style: italic;
	}

	.teacher-figure {
		margin: 0;
	}

	.teacher-portrait {
		width: 100%;
		aspect-ratio: 1;
	}

	.teacher-portrait img {
		width: 100%;
		height: 100%;
		object-fit: cover;
		object-position: center 28%;
	}

	.book-plate {
		display: block;
		width: 100%;
		max-width: 11rem;
		transition:
			border-color var(--dur-hover) var(--ease-standard),
			scale var(--dur-press) var(--ease-standard);
	}

	/* A whisper of lift and press so the plate reads as a link, not a print. */
	.book-plate:active {
		scale: var(--press-scale);
	}

	@media (hover: hover) and (pointer: fine) {
		/* A shadow won't read on midnight — brighten the plate edge instead. */
		.book-plate:hover {
			border-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--ink-on-dark) 60%, transparent);
		}
	}

	.book-plate img {
		width: 100%;
		display: block;
	}

	.book-quote {
		margin: clamp(3rem, 4vw + 1rem, 5rem) 0 0;
		max-width: 44rem;
	}

	.book-quote blockquote {
		font-family: var(--font-serif);
		font-style: italic;
		font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 1.05rem + 1.6vw, 2.1rem);
		line-height: 1.4;
		letter-spacing: -0.01em;
		color: var(--ink-on-dark);
		margin: 0;
	}

	.book-quote figcaption {
		margin-top: 1rem;
		font-family: var(--font-sans);
		font-size: var(--fs-metadata);
		color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--ink-on-dark) 76%, transparent);
	}

	@media (max-width: 52rem) {
		.teacher-layout {
			grid-template-columns: 1fr;
			padding-right: 0;
		}

		/* Both plates share one height; the book keeps its 2:3 ratio, so the
		   pair reads as a centered pair of prints. The size formula keeps
		   portrait + book + gap inside the viewport on narrow phones. */
		.teacher-media {
			--plate-size: min(11rem, calc((100vw - 6.5rem) * 0.6));
			grid-template-columns: auto auto;
			justify-content: center;
			gap: 1.5rem 2.5rem;
			align-items: start;
			/* With the copy's 1rem paragraph margin this matches the 3rem the
			   book quote leaves below the block. */
			margin-top: 2rem;
		}

		.teacher-portrait {
			width: var(--plate-size);
		}

		/* The figure matches the cover's width (348:522 cover at plate height),
		   so the caption wraps and centers within the image edges — one unit. */
		.teacher-figure--book {
			width: calc(var(--plate-size) * 348 / 522);
		}

		.book-plate {
			max-width: none;
			width: 100%;
			height: var(--plate-size);
		}

		.book-plate img {
			width: 100%;
			height: 100%;
			object-fit: cover;
		}
	}
</style>
